1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Tuesday morning, leadership says the problem is fixed.
They add one RACI row.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,000
Resolve invoice exception.
AP: Responsible. Procurement: Accountable.
Operations: Consulted. Finance: Informed.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,100
The agent routes the case to Procurement.

4
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:25,600
“I own the supplier relationship.
I am not authorized to release payment.”

5
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:34,000
AP can block payment, but cannot accept the variance.
Finance owns the control, but was only informed.
Operations still sees a 48-hour supply risk.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,300
The cast is named. The decision is not.

7
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:46,300
A RACI can clarify participation.
An agent also needs an executable decision contract.

8
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:55,500
Trigger · Evidence · Recommender · Decider
Executor · Authority limit · Escalation · Decision record

9
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:04,000
Pick one real exception. Ask who recommends, decides,
executes, under what limit, and using what evidence.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
If the answers live only in people’s heads,
the agent may execute one unwritten interpretation faster.
